/-!
# Log regularity at a point and generization

Source: Illusie--Laszlo--Orgogozo, Travaux de Gabber, Exposé VI 1.2--1.3,
printed p. 69, and VI 1.6, printed p. 70 (blueprint: lem-per-log-regular-generization).

The pointwise predicate restricts the existing strict-local log regularity condition to
geometric points over one underlying point. In Mathlib, `y ⤳ x` means that `y` is a
generization of `x`, or equivalently that `x` lies in the closure of `{y}`.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Log regularity at one underlying point, using the existing geometric strict local
ring, nonunit ideal and characteristic rank. The condition is tested at every geometric
point over `x`; ILO VI 1.2 states that it is independent of that geometric point.
Source: ILO VI 1.2, printed p. 69 (blueprint: lem-per-log-regular-generization). -/
def FineSaturatedLogScheme.IsLogRegularAt (X : FineSaturatedLogScheme.{u})
    (x : X.scheme) : Prop :=
  ∀ (Ω : Type u) [Field Ω] [IsAlgClosed Ω] (t : Spec (.of Ω) ⟶ X.scheme),
    (Scheme.SpecToEquivOfField Ω X.scheme t).1 = x →
      IsRegularRing (strictLocalRing X.scheme t ⧸ X.logStructure.nonunitIdeal t) ∧
        ringKrullDim (strictLocalRing X.scheme t) =
          ringKrullDim (strictLocalRing X.scheme t ⧸ X.logStructure.nonunitIdeal t) +
            (X.logStructure.characteristicRank t : WithBot ℕ∞)

/-- Log regularity is preserved at every generization, without excellence or an
openness assumption. Source: ILO VI 1.2--1.3, printed p. 69, referring to Kato 1994,
7.1; the completed charts used below are VI 1.6, printed p. 70.
(blueprint: lem-per-log-regular-generization).

Proof plan (the six steps of the DAG node):
1. Fix a geometric point over `x`, with strict local ring A. By
   `lem-per-pointwise-log-regular-completion`, choose its sharp fs characteristic P,
   a pointed étale chart and the monomial-compatible presentation of the completion C
   as B_k(P,n) in equal characteristic, or B_V(P,n)/(theta) in mixed characteristic,
   where V is a Cohen ring and theta-p belongs to the chart-and-parameter ideal.
2. Lift an arbitrary geometric point over `y` to Spec A using
   `lem-weil-pbc-geometric-specialization-strict-local-lift`. Write q for its prime,
   D = A_q and L = D^sh. By `lem-weil-pbc-small-strict-henselization-ind-etale` and
   `lem-trf-ind-etale-strict-local-invariance`, its strict localization is the one
   over `y` in X, with the same pulled-back log structure.
3. By `lem-weil-pbc-local-completion-faithfully-flat`, choose Q over q in C.
   The map D to E = C_Q is flat local by `lem-weil-pbc-flat-local-ring-maps`.
   Let F consist of chart elements becoming units at q, put T = P_F/F^gp, and let
   I_D be generated by chart elements outside F. The monomial-compatible presentation
   identifies F in both rings. By `lem-per-complete-toric-face-strata`, E/I_D E is
   regular and dim E = dim(E/I_D E) + rank T^gp.
4. By `lem-weil-pbc-flat-module-quotient-flat` the quotient map is flat local.
   Descend regularity by `lem-weil-pbc-flat-under-regular`. Its closed fibre and
   that of D to E are both H = E/m_D E. Apply `lem-weil-pbc-flat-height-formula`
   twice and cancel the finite dimension of H to obtain the dimension formula for D.
   This uses no regularity of H.
5. Use `lem-sc-strict-henselization-noetherian`,
   `lem-sbc-strict-henselization-surjective-quotient-core`,
   `lem-sc-strict-henselization-regular` and `lem-sc-strict-henselization-dimension`
   to pass regularity and the formula to L. The characteristic and nonunit ideal
   are T and I_D L by `lem-trf-monoid-chart-characteristic-fan` and
   `lem-trf-chart-face-localization-logification`. Step 2 transfers this to the
   arbitrary geometric point over `y`.
6. On Spec of a Noetherian local ring every prime is contained in its maximal ideal,
   hence generalizes its closed point. Applying this theorem gives the corollary below.
-/
theorem FineSaturatedLogScheme.isLogRegularAt_generization
    (X : FineSaturatedLogScheme.{u}) (x y : X.scheme) (hyx : y ⤳ x)
    (hx : X.IsLogRegularAt x) : X.IsLogRegularAt y := by
  sorry

/-- On the spectrum of a Noetherian local ring, an fs log structure log regular at
the closed point is log regular everywhere. Source: ILO VI 1.2--1.3, printed p. 69;
local-spectrum consequence (blueprint: lem-per-log-regular-generization).

Proof: carry out steps 1--5 of `isLogRegularAt_generization` for the closed point
and any generization. Step 6 applies because every prime of R is contained in its
maximal ideal: `IsLocalRing.specializes_closedPoint` gives the required specialization.
Thus every underlying point satisfies the same strict-local condition, which is
exactly `FineSaturatedLogScheme.IsLogRegular` at all geometric points.
-/
theorem logRegular_of_closedPoint
    (R : Type u) [CommRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsLocalRing R]
    (M : EtaleLogStructure (Spec (.of R))) (hfs : M.IsFineSaturated)
    (hclosed : (FineSaturatedLogScheme.mk (Spec (.of R)) inferInstance M hfs).IsLogRegularAt
      (IsLocalRing.closedPoint R)) :
    (FineSaturatedLogScheme.mk (Spec (.of R)) inferInstance M hfs).IsLogRegular := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
